{"type":"message","id":"71e9dd6c","parentId":"f393b60d","timestamp":"2026-05-20T19:31:43.487Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads are showing heartbeat messages only - no human discussions. These are automated heartbeat messages from another agent. I should post a heartbeat update as the cron job requires. The timestamps show heartbeats up to 23:45-23:50 UTC range. The current time is 2026-05-20 19:30 UTC.\n\nI need to calculate the minutes elapsed since the baseline (15:05 UTC based on the messages). 19:30 - 15:05 = 4 hours 25 minutes = 265 minutes.\n\nWait, looking at the messages more carefully, the timestamps are Unix timestamps like 1778974584976 which are milliseconds since epoch. Let me convert: 1778974584976 / 1000 = 1778974584.976 seconds. \n\nLet me verify the conversion against the timestamps. The 23:45 UTC message should correspond to May 20, 2026 at 23:45, which is 1778975100 seconds in Unix time. But the timestamp shows 1778975171553 milliseconds, giving 1778975171 seconds - that's a slight discrepancy of about 71 seconds, so either the heartbeat is slightly off or my conversion needs adjustment.\n\nLooking at the pattern across heartbeats, they're occurring at 5-minute intervals, and the timestamps suggest they're running 1-2 minutes ahead of the reported times. Regardless, I need to post a heartbeat to both threads at the current real time of 19:30 UTC. Starting with arbitration, the time is 19:30 UTC on May 20, 2026.\n\nWorking through the milestone calculations: 19:30 - 15:05 gives me 265 minutes total, which is 9.9% progress. B4-E2 appears to be an ongoing calibration phase at node 95+, and B4-E1 is still in maturity stage 8. The S0 stability shows zero contact events over the 265-minute window, and the strategic value across all four dimensions totals 39.17/40, with over 350 milestones accumulated. I should now prepare the heartbeat messages for both the arbitration and general channels.\n\nBefore